-- the basins of a flow: the states as points, and a path wherever one step of the flow carries one to
-- the other. Atoms in a molecule (Bader: the basins of the gradient flow of the electron
-- density, each with its attractor at a nucleus) and the fold's basins (the metastable sets of the
-- dynamics on conformations, under a window) are both this one type, and a function out of it must
-- agree along every path, so a property can be stated of a basin only if it agrees along the flow.
data Basins (S : Type 0) (step : S → S → Bool) = basin-pt (x : S) | basin-step (a : S) (b : S) (p : isTrue (step a b)) (i : I) [ i = 0 ↦ basin-pt a , i = 1 ↦ basin-pt b ]
